From b5e73f17968bd90458f3b202a08105654be0c0f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arbion Halili <a.halili@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 17:12:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(cli): build and serve a shared metadata index
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Expose the shared index on the two virtio-fs command surfaces. `snix
store index` and `snix castore index` build one — the former over the
store paths a PathInfoService lists, reading the `nix-support/fsmeta`
declaration convention; the latter over the children of a directory,
which carry no convention — and write it atomically. `snix store
virtiofs` and `snix castore virtiofs` gain `--metadata-index PATH`, which
attaches it so several daemons over the same content map one copy of the
metadata through the host page cache instead of each replicating it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I96f9ff0702f6a178e12e8654dd5cf65f44912686
---
